  "goodToKnow": "Die Zivilisation is civilisation: die westliche Zivilisation, zurück in die Zivilisation. Zivilisationskrankheiten are lifestyle diseases such as diabetes and heart disease. German thinkers long contrasted Zivilisation (outward, technical progress) with Kultur (inner, spiritual refinement), a contrast that Thomas Mann and others made much of around the First World War. Zivilisiert means civilised. From Latin civis (citizen)."
